%N A402677 Numbers whose powerful part (A057521) is an Achilles number (A052486).
%C A402677 First differs from A072412 at n = 111. Differs from A072412 by having the terms 43200, 72000, 84672, ..., and not having the terms 5184, 11664, 25920, ... .
%C A402677 Numbers whose prime factorization exponents that are greater than 1 have a greatest common divisor that equals 1.
%C A402677 The asymptotic density of this sequence is Sum_{m>=1} mu(m) * (d(m) - 1/zeta(2)) = 0.022525060738090906154..., where mu is the Möbius function (A008683), d(m) = zeta(m) * Product_{p prime} (1 - 1/p^2 - 1/p^(m+1) + 1/p^(m+2)) for m >= 2, and d(1) = 1.
%H A402677 Amiram Eldar, <a href="/A402677/b402677.txt">Table of n, a(n) for n = 1..10000</a>
%H A402677 <a href="/index/Eu#epf">Index entries for sequences computed from exponents in factorization of n</a>.
%H A402677 <a href="/index/Pow#powerful">Index entries for sequences related to powerful numbers</a>.
%t A402677 q[k_] := Module[{e = Select[FactorInteger[k][[;; , 2]], # > 1 &]}, Length[e] > 0 && GCD @@ e == 1]; Select[Range[2300], q]
%o A402677 (PARI) isok(k) = {my(e = select(x -> x > 1, factor(k)[, 2])); #e > 0 && gcd(e) == 1;}
%Y A402677 Complement of A398824 within A013929.
